  "summary": "With those model choices, the TARGET defines exactly the stated impossibility claim: it excludes every dependency cycle, including a self-loop, and requires one candidate twin to match at all finite lengths. The passage comparison is accurate as the author’s interpretation: Doerig et al. contrast feedforward and recurrent systems without explicitly defining the no-self-loop criterion, while Hanson and Walker describe self-dependence in the first component, which alone violates that criterion."
